{"@type":"Process","@id":"30c87121-36fc-3209-acd4-16a8e3262ab4","name":"Aluminum, ingot/slab; remelt and direct chill casting; at plant","description":"This gate-to-gate process represents the production of direct chill (DC) cast aluminum ingot from external and internal aluminum scrap and primary and secondary aluminum ingots. The dataset has a recycled content of 73% which reflects the average recycled content of North American aluminum ingot used for can sheet manufacturing in 2016. Aluminum ingot is an intermediate product used as an input to subsequent manufacturing steps. The process produces no co-products.","category":"31-33: Manufacturing/3313: Alumina and Aluminum Production and Processing","version":"01.00.005","lastChange":"2026-09-24T17:15:54Z","processType":"UNIT_PROCESS","defaultAllocationMethod":"PHYSICAL_ALLOCATION","isInfrastructureProcess":false,"location":{"@type":"Location","@id":"0b3b97fa-6688-3c56-88ee-4ae80ec0c3c2","name":"United States of America (the)","category":"Country"},"processDocumentation":{"validFrom":"2015-01-01","validUntil":"2016-12-31","timeDescription":"Emissions data reflects 2015. Energy data reflects 2016","geographyDescription":"U.S. and Canada","technologyDescription":"Scrap, primary and secondary ingots are melted in a melting furnace and cast into ingots using the direct chill method.","inventoryMethodDescription":"Attributional","modelingConstantsDescription":"Water vapor is excluded from the inventory","completenessDescription":"CUTOFF flows act as placeholders for several waste flows without available techosphere data. A mass balance was performed on the foreground unit process by the original data developers and no flows were knowlingly omitted.","dataSelectionDescription":"Primary data was collected from U.S., Canadian and international producers that supply the North American market. Data providers reflect \u003e95% of production in the target region.","dataTreatmentDescription":"Inventory data was pulled directly 